[{:db/id 17592186162105 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-70462da6-df40-572c-b721-518f7d0fb229" "question-b1e5d993-4954-596b-9a63-c575f6c7babb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-70462da6-df40-572c-b721-518f7d0fb229" :question/id #uuid "70462da6-df40-572c-b721-518f7d0fb229" :question/math-academy-id "q-142893" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{Y|X}(0\\,|\\,1)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(0\\,|\\,1)=P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=1).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=0\\,|\\,X=1)=\\frac{P(X=1,Y=0)}{P(X=1)}=\\frac{f(1,0)}{{f}_{X}(1)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(1) & =f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(1,2) \\\\  & =0.25+0.1+0.25 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(1,0)=0.25.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{X}(1)=0.6$ and $f(1,0)=0.25$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(0\\,|\\,1) & =P(Y=0\\,|\\,X=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1,0)}{{f}_{X}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.25}{0.6} \\\\  & ≈0.42.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38673cd4-d233-5042-adf0-a6d70114ec93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38673cd4-d233-5042-adf0-a6d70114ec93" :answer-field/id #uuid "38673cd4-d233-5042-adf0-a6d70114ec93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb1bcdc1-72d1-5f68-bb9d-cd8c02cd1c36" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1106665-3f25-50f6-bf70-205dfb7d3993" "answer-4deb08c4-9a80-57d4-8a91-17d29d971092" "answer-461964e4-b6e1-5a7d-85c6-1b999a2b0407" "answer-cb1bcdc1-72d1-5f68-bb9d-cd8c02cd1c36" "answer-4176ad50-617b-5bbe-9749-530c4518c952"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1106665-3f25-50f6-bf70-205dfb7d3993" :answer/id #uuid "d1106665-3f25-50f6-bf70-205dfb7d3993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4deb08c4-9a80-57d4-8a91-17d29d971092" :answer/id #uuid "4deb08c4-9a80-57d4-8a91-17d29d971092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-461964e4-b6e1-5a7d-85c6-1b999a2b0407" :answer/id #uuid "461964e4-b6e1-5a7d-85c6-1b999a2b0407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.37" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb1bcdc1-72d1-5f68-bb9d-cd8c02cd1c36" :answer/id #uuid "cb1bcdc1-72d1-5f68-bb9d-cd8c02cd1c36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4176ad50-617b-5bbe-9749-530c4518c952" :answer/id #uuid "4176ad50-617b-5bbe-9749-530c4518c952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162077 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b172bfa5-07a0-5df8-8d2d-99d558ae1db4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b172bfa5-07a0-5df8-8d2d-99d558ae1db4" :question/id #uuid "b172bfa5-07a0-5df8-8d2d-99d558ae1db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-142896" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.25$ | $0$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=9$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(0<X\\le 6\\,|\\,Y=3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 6\\,|\\,Y=3) & =\\frac{P((0<X\\le 6),Y=3)}{P(Y=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=3,Y=3)+P(X=6,Y=3)}{P(Y=3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,3)+f(6,3)}{{f}_{Y}(3)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(3) & =f(0,3)+f(3,3)+f(6,3)+f(9,3) \\\\  & =0+0.1+0+0.1 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(3,3)=0.1$ and $f(6,3)=0.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 6\\,|\\,Y=3) & =\\frac{f(3,3)+f(6,3)}{{f}_{Y}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1+0}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-395c93a7-3493-526c-8001-2fe1cf196ffc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-395c93a7-3493-526c-8001-2fe1cf196ffc" :answer-field/id #uuid "395c93a7-3493-526c-8001-2fe1cf196ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d82990b6-7322-5310-a01d-936be990fc20" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3b9f3ed-06e4-59ef-8471-d8398ce14731" "answer-f4c7c149-9c87-52d8-aaf5-4888360f519e" "answer-d82990b6-7322-5310-a01d-936be990fc20" "answer-1dea9c6c-8a37-5b15-a053-45fd4f8d2f9f" "answer-f7a8127b-532b-5c4e-95ea-e82e38e362d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3b9f3ed-06e4-59ef-8471-d8398ce14731" :answer/id #uuid "c3b9f3ed-06e4-59ef-8471-d8398ce14731" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4c7c149-9c87-52d8-aaf5-4888360f519e" :answer/id #uuid "f4c7c149-9c87-52d8-aaf5-4888360f519e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d82990b6-7322-5310-a01d-936be990fc20" :answer/id #uuid "d82990b6-7322-5310-a01d-936be990fc20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dea9c6c-8a37-5b15-a053-45fd4f8d2f9f" :answer/id #uuid "1dea9c6c-8a37-5b15-a053-45fd4f8d2f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7a8127b-532b-5c4e-95ea-e82e38e362d5" :answer/id #uuid "f7a8127b-532b-5c4e-95ea-e82e38e362d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1e5d993-4954-596b-9a63-c575f6c7babb" :question/id #uuid "b1e5d993-4954-596b-9a63-c575f6c7babb" :question/math-academy-id "q-142903" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{32}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{32}$ | $\\frac{3}{32}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{5}{32}$ | $\\frac{5}{32}$ | $\\frac{3}{32}$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{Y|X}(3\\,|\\,3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(3\\,|\\,3)=P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=3).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=3\\,|\\,X=3)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=3)}{P(X=3)}=\\frac{f(3,3)}{{f}_{X}(3)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,1)+f(3,2)+f(3,3) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{32}+\\frac{5}{32}+\\frac{3}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(3,3)=\\frac{3}{32}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{X}(3)=\\frac{13}{32}$ and $f(3,3)=\\frac{3}{32}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(3\\,|\\,3) & =P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=3) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,3)}{{f}_{X}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{32})}{(\\frac{13}{32})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b9630d02-fcc6-50aa-af4a-264fb35a6574"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b9630d02-fcc6-50aa-af4a-264fb35a6574" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9630d02-fcc6-50aa-af4a-264fb35a6574" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-500b7039-9773-5a4d-a57b-2ec78d1c6cc4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36eae30e-fa0d-5135-a62d-0465c3393122" "answer-7f2cbc96-2672-5c50-abb6-ff77349a1002" "answer-500b7039-9773-5a4d-a57b-2ec78d1c6cc4" "answer-b71aacf7-31c6-5c18-bf8d-c7c655c001fb" "answer-568228f9-502e-5052-aae6-cf24f3f3e87c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36eae30e-fa0d-5135-a62d-0465c3393122" :answer/id #uuid "36eae30e-fa0d-5135-a62d-0465c3393122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f2cbc96-2672-5c50-abb6-ff77349a1002" :answer/id #uuid "7f2cbc96-2672-5c50-abb6-ff77349a1002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-500b7039-9773-5a4d-a57b-2ec78d1c6cc4" :answer/id #uuid "500b7039-9773-5a4d-a57b-2ec78d1c6cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b71aacf7-31c6-5c18-bf8d-c7c655c001fb" :answer/id #uuid "b71aacf7-31c6-5c18-bf8d-c7c655c001fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-568228f9-502e-5052-aae6-cf24f3f3e87c" :answer/id #uuid "568228f9-502e-5052-aae6-cf24f3f3e87c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162104 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-51c80586-803f-589a-a591-22c79fbdc1d5" "question-9f027a74-2cf2-5941-ad79-db682e13a988"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-51c80586-803f-589a-a591-22c79fbdc1d5" :question/id #uuid "51c80586-803f-589a-a591-22c79fbdc1d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-142943" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=3)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=y\\,|\\,X=3)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=y)}{P(X=3)}=\\frac{f(3,y)}{{f}_{X}(3)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.55$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $y\\in {1,2,3},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=1\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,1)}{{f}_{X}(3)}=\\frac{0.4}{0.6}=\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ P(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{X}(3)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.6}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=3) & =\\frac{f(3,3)}{{f}_{X}(3)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.6}=\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e2be8906-c901-5824-8831-8ec5b219586c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e2be8906-c901-5824-8831-8ec5b219586c" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2be8906-c901-5824-8831-8ec5b219586c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-57efad21-b751-5436-bc49-9e31dc13e0c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6cfd22a8-559a-59b7-b153-5dfd12c90df1" "answer-309c4fa5-1b46-51a0-8421-56fe01cf985c" "answer-0c15b04c-20e5-50a7-9307-de1f9df589c6" "answer-57efad21-b751-5436-bc49-9e31dc13e0c3" "answer-74305b04-7264-5ad2-accf-85820a02cffa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cfd22a8-559a-59b7-b153-5dfd12c90df1" :answer/id #uuid "6cfd22a8-559a-59b7-b153-5dfd12c90df1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-309c4fa5-1b46-51a0-8421-56fe01cf985c" :answer/id #uuid "309c4fa5-1b46-51a0-8421-56fe01cf985c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c15b04c-20e5-50a7-9307-de1f9df589c6" :answer/id #uuid "0c15b04c-20e5-50a7-9307-de1f9df589c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57efad21-b751-5436-bc49-9e31dc13e0c3" :answer/id #uuid "57efad21-b751-5436-bc49-9e31dc13e0c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74305b04-7264-5ad2-accf-85820a02cffa" :answer/id #uuid "74305b04-7264-5ad2-accf-85820a02cffa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9f027a74-2cf2-5941-ad79-db682e13a988" :question/id #uuid "9f027a74-2cf2-5941-ad79-db682e13a988" :question/math-academy-id "q-142945" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)=\\frac{P(X=x,Y=4)}{P(Y=4)}=\\frac{f(x,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $x\\in {1,2,3},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(2,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.05}{0.2}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ P(X=3\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(3,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.05}{0.2}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-970267c4-5873-5e3f-8e48-19af831de5c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-970267c4-5873-5e3f-8e48-19af831de5c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "970267c4-5873-5e3f-8e48-19af831de5c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eb5e3e81-5bff-5014-b439-496be93167e0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb5e3e81-5bff-5014-b439-496be93167e0" "answer-d6519b1a-e3ae-5f03-a15a-752660368763" "answer-0edd7b5b-c6e3-57a4-8be5-217568bb3909" "answer-5d0c9436-13dd-5557-a695-bb3800789fbf" "answer-ebb9920f-ffe3-53da-b1aa-afd4167bb93d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb5e3e81-5bff-5014-b439-496be93167e0" :answer/id #uuid "eb5e3e81-5bff-5014-b439-496be93167e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6519b1a-e3ae-5f03-a15a-752660368763" :answer/id #uuid "d6519b1a-e3ae-5f03-a15a-752660368763" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0edd7b5b-c6e3-57a4-8be5-217568bb3909" :answer/id #uuid "0edd7b5b-c6e3-57a4-8be5-217568bb3909" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d0c9436-13dd-5557-a695-bb3800789fbf" :answer/id #uuid "5d0c9436-13dd-5557-a695-bb3800789fbf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebb9920f-ffe3-53da-b1aa-afd4167bb93d" :answer/id #uuid "ebb9920f-ffe3-53da-b1aa-afd4167bb93d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4f58fa0a-3eab-578c-8ede-b29945f6d461" :activity/id #uuid "4f58fa0a-3eab-578c-8ede-b29945f6d461" :activity/title "Conditional Distributions for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049149 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-dacbdc7c-ec48-5db6-8025-bca188ffb47d" "step-b0812b16-60e1-5ebb-80af-c271cd3f189c" "step-21b7e9f5-9b6f-59bb-8de5-73acd87de7ec" "step-30942c86-dbc3-5faa-928f-8a3e27c6ef2a" "step-e7c09165-5bb0-5525-a272-3f6aee4bdcee"] :activity/first-step "step-dacbdc7c-ec48-5db6-8025-bca188ffb47d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-dacbdc7c-ec48-5db6-8025-bca188ffb47d" :step/id #uuid "dacbdc7c-ec48-5db6-8025-bca188ffb47d" :step/content "question-70462da6-df40-572c-b721-518f7d0fb229" :step/next "step-b0812b16-60e1-5ebb-80af-c271cd3f189c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b0812b16-60e1-5ebb-80af-c271cd3f189c" :step